From bdaec981fc0418c623cbbec218e91f94e0be43dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 17:26:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 475/572] fix(stm32mp2): flush cache at the beginning of
 bl2_el3_plat_prepare_exit

The data cache has been disabled in the bl2_run_next_image(), the caller
function of bl2_el3_plat_prepare_exit(). We were already flushing the
data cache for storage data before calling stm32mp_io_exit(). But this
should be done at the beginning of bl2_el3_plat_prepare_exit().
Else some data may not be correct in memory.
Sometimes, in trusted boot and when Cortex-M33 was TDCID, the board
failed to boot with a synchronous exception. This was because timer_ops
structure was not correct in memory, and timer operations are used in
PSA functions called by rse_platform_stm32_share_key_stop(). Flushing
the cache before solves the issue.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 49c20d215b96c20687645fa59c4a7588c610fd05 fix(stm32mp2): flush cache at the beginning of bl2_el3_plat_prepare_exit]
Change-Id: Idcb3fe1722932d131f9fc8832105a1cc3ffaf558
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/575558
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
---
 plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c b/plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c
index da5d14a6a7..68b928f040 100644
--- a/plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c
+++ b/plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 /*
- * Copyright (c) 2023-2025, STMicroelectronics - All Rights Reserved
+ * Copyright (c) 2023-2026, STMicroelectronics - All Rights Reserved
  *
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
  */
@@ -869,6 +869,15 @@ int bl2_plat_handle_post_image_load(unsigned int image_id)
 
 void bl2_el3_plat_prepare_exit(void)
 {
+	/*
+	 * The cache has just been disabled by the caller function.
+	 * The flush of the data sections should then be done at the beginning
+	 * of this function before accessing data that have not been flushed.
+	 * This is the case for the storage data, or the timer ops for example.
+	 */
+	flush_dcache_range(BSS_START, BSS_END - BSS_START);
+	flush_dcache_range(DATA_START, DATA_END - DATA_START);
+
 #if STM32MP_M33_TDCID
 #if TRUSTED_BOARD_BOOT
 	if (rse_platform_stm32_share_key_stop(0) != PSA_SUCCESS) {
@@ -881,9 +890,6 @@ void bl2_el3_plat_prepare_exit(void)
 	}
 #endif
 
-	flush_dcache_range(BSS_START, BSS_END - BSS_START);
-	flush_dcache_range(DATA_START, DATA_END - DATA_START);
-
 	stm32mp_io_exit();
 
 	/* Unmask potential tamper before exit */
